   "id": "seg-01",
   "spk": "Alex",
   "en": "This morning, a security alert arrives. I explain the phishing to a new teammate. We discuss the risk around the malware. I document the security advisory so the team can review it later. If the Dependabot alert fails, we need a clear plan. Priya checks with me, \"I'd like to transfer money.\" I answer clearly, \"Has the payment gone through?\" I check my notes and confirm the next step.",
   "tts": "This morning, a security alert arrives. I explain the phishing to a new teammate. We discuss the risk around the malware. I document the security advisory so the team can review it later. If the depend a bot alert fails, we need a clear plan. Priya checks with me, \"I'd like to transfer money.\" I answer clearly, \"Has the payment gone through?\" I check my notes and confirm the next step.",
   "audio_file": "audio/seg-01.mp3",
   "zh": "今天早上，一个安全警报来了。我向一位新队友解释了网络钓鱼。我们讨论了恶意软件相关的风险。我把安全公告写成文档，方便团队之后查看。如果Dependabot 警报失败，我们需要一个清晰的方案。Priya向我确认：\"我想转账。\"我清楚地回答：\"付款成功了吗？\"我检查笔记，确认了下一步。",
   "hard": [
    {
     "w": "phishing",
     "type": "term",
     "def": "网络钓鱼，用假消息诱骗用户交出敏感信息"
    },
    {
     "w": "malware",
     "type": "term",
     "def": "恶意软件，故意破坏或窃取数据的软件"
    },
    {
     "w": "I'd like to transfer money.",
     "type": "term",
     "def": "我想转账。"
    },
    {
     "w": "Has the payment gone through?",
     "type": "term",
     "def": "付款成功了吗？"
    },
    {
     "w": "security advisory",
     "type": "term",
     "def": "安全公告，披露漏洞影响和修复方法的通知"
    },
    {
     "w": "Dependabot alert",
     "type": "term",
     "def": "Dependabot 警报，GitHub 对依赖漏洞的自动提醒"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "seg-02",
   "spk": "Alex",
   "en": "I check a strange charge at the bank. Before we part, Leo says, \"I don't recognize this charge.\" I answer, \"My card was declined.\" I document the security patch so the team can review it later. If the suspicious link fails, we need a clear plan. I suggest that we check the vulnerable dependency first. The result depends on the security update, so I check it twice. The team agrees on the plan, and I record the decision.",
   "tts": "I check a strange charge at the bank. Before we part, Leo says, \"I don't recognize this charge.\" I answer, \"My card was declined.\" I document the security patch so the team can review it later. If the suspicious link fails, we need a clear plan. I suggest that we check the vulnerable dependency first. The result depends on the security update, so I check it twice. The team agrees on the plan, and I record the decision.",
   "audio_file": "audio/seg-02.mp3",
   "zh": "我在银行核查了一笔可疑的扣款。分开前，Leo说：\"我不认识这笔扣款。\"我回答：\"我的卡被拒绝了。\"我把安全补丁写成文档，方便团队之后查看。如果可疑链接失败，我们需要一个清晰的方案。我建议我们先检查易受攻击的依赖。结果取决于安全更新，所以我检查了两遍。团队就计划达成一致，我记录了决定。",
   "hard": [
    {
